 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "FAtlsmZFcFYJ",
   "from": "Herbert Jägle",
   "author": "ff42271ef6191bca",
   "date": "2013-02-03T13:13:42Z",
   "subject": "ggsave always opens a graphics window on Mac OS",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi All,<br><br>i am using R console on Mac OSX to run R scripts. I use two different methods to create plot files:<br><br>either:<br>----------<br>pdf(file=&#39;name.pdf&#39;)<br>grid.arrange(p)<br>dev.off()<br>----------<br>or<br>ggsave(filename=&#39;name.pdf&#39;, plot=p)<br><br>While the first just creates the plot file, the use of ggsave always opens a graphics window (which stays blank) and then creates the plot file.<br>Looks like ggsave opens the standard device prior to identification of the desired file type.<br><br>Is it possible to tell ggsave not to open the default device?<br><br>Thanks,<br>Herbert<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "5SNZNB16nXAJ",
   "from": "Herbert Jägle",
   "author": "ff42271ef6191bca",
   "date": "2013-02-03T21:38:09Z",
   "subject": "Re: ggsave always opens a graphics window on Mac OS",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Just in case someone else is searching for this issue. I received an email with a, for me surprising, simple solution:<br><br><div><span>It won&#39;t show if you type the desired width and height:</span></div><div><span>ggsave(filename=&#39;name.pdf&#39;, plot=p,w=6,h=4)<br></span></div><div> </div>Thanks,<br>Herbert"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><br>On Sunday, February 3, 2013 2:13:42 PM UTC+1, Herbert Jägle wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hi All,<br><br>i am using R console on Mac OSX to run R scripts. I use two different methods to create plot files:<br><br>either:<br>----------<br>pdf(file=&#39;name.pdf&#39;)<br>grid.arrange(p)<br>dev.off()<br>----------<br>or<br>ggsave(filename=&#39;name.pdf&#39;, plot=p)<br><br>While the first just creates the plot file, the use of ggsave always opens a graphics window (which stays blank) and then creates the plot file.<br>Looks like ggsave opens the standard device prior to identification of the desired file type.<br><br>Is it possible to tell ggsave not to open the default device?<br><br>Thanks,<br>Herbert<br></blockquote>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "xz8PjlR4KMEJ",
